"help_start_title" = "Connect your devices";
"help_start_body" = "Start receiving on your other device and keep both devices on a network where they can reach each other. Pair from Receiver and check the device names on both screens. A familiar name helps you recognize a device; pairing establishes trust.";
"help_scope_title" = "Choose what to back up";
"help_scope_body" = "Select items in Library for a manual backup. In backup settings, new-photo backup and historical import are separate controls: enable new-photo backup for future additions, and start historical import to include existing accessible photos and videos. Supported motion photos include their photo and video components; accessible burst frames are included together.";
"help_receipt_title" = "What received means";
"help_receipt_body" = "A received task has a verification receipt from the paired receiver. It does not confirm that another service has backed it up or that a receiver-side conversion has finished. Keep your source originals until you have checked the receiver’s storage and retention rules. PhotoBridge does not delete items from your Apple photo library.";
"help_recover_title" = "When backup stops";
"help_recover_body" = "Check that backup is not paused, the receiver is running, and both devices can reach each other. Reopen PhotoBridge to continue scheduling work. In Backup, open tasks needing attention and read the error before retrying. Keep the existing pairing and task history when recovering a connection; deleting app data is not a recovery step.";
"help_permission_title" = "Missing photos";
"help_permission_body" = "PhotoBridge can only read photos you allow. Check Photos access in system settings, including the selected items if access is limited. Originals stored only in iCloud need a network connection and local staging space before upload. Granting access does not itself start a historical import.";
"help_space_title" = "When storage is low";
"help_space_body" = "Local cache holds prepared files while they are being transferred. Increase its budget only if the sending device has room. If the receiver is full, manage space on that device and then retry. Removing a staged file or a receiver copy is not proof of backup; use the app’s storage controls rather than deleting its internal files.";
"help_support_title" = "Collect useful diagnostics";
"help_support_body" = "Open Settings → Diagnostics → Activity log to inspect and export events. Include the time of the problem, the task’s displayed state, and whether the app was in the foreground or background. Review the exported report before sharing it.";
